{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Vayemariruhu.</b> The Nagid said that its meaning is: they embittered him, like מטרה (a target), and afterward the archers shot. So too: \"Proclaim to Babylon many [archers]\" (Jeremiah 50:29)." "And similarly the sense of vayemariruhu: \"My assailants surround me\" (Job 16:13), at the end of: \"He pours out to the earth my merirati.\"" "<b>Vayistemuho.</b> It is set earlier, before vayemariruhu, as though he said: and moreover, they hated him. And this is an allusion to his brothers, who sold him."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {0 "Resolved 'הנגיד' as the Nagid; the specific individual (likely Samuel ha-Nagid) is not named in the text."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:34.763727785Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}